WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:05.625
- "If we encounter a
man of rare intellect,

00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:08.234
"we should ask him what books he reads."

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:09.901
Ralph Waldo Emerson.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:10.935
Hi, I'm Evan Carmichael,

00:00:10.935 --> 00:00:12.564
and today I'm going to share

00:00:12.564 --> 00:00:16.314
the seven books every
entrepreneur must read.

00:00:17.224 --> 00:00:18.697
These are seven books that have had

00:00:18.697 --> 00:00:21.026
a tremendous impact on my life,

00:00:21.026 --> 00:00:22.765
how I think about business,

00:00:22.765 --> 00:00:24.882
and I hope they have
the same impact on you.

00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:27.383
Now, I used to have a ton of books.

00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:30.306
I used to have walls and walls of books,

00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:31.601
and when I saw something interesting,

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:32.700
I would pick it up and buy it.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.738
Somebody told me they'd get it.

00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:34.571
I would buy.

00:00:34.571 --> 00:00:36.120
And I found I had all of these books

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.518
just sitting on the
shelves, collecting dust,

00:00:38.518 --> 00:00:42.212
and I was accumulating more
books than I could read.

00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:43.813
And I had great intentions to read them,

00:00:43.813 --> 00:00:45.515
but I never got around to them

00:00:45.515 --> 00:00:47.534
and it created stress.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.686
It created stress looking
at all these books

00:00:49.686 --> 00:00:51.341
and knowing I got to
read all of these things.

00:00:51.341 --> 00:00:53.877
So, I decided one day I
would get rid of them all,

00:00:53.877 --> 00:00:55.957
and I donated them to a local library

00:00:55.957 --> 00:00:56.802
and I pared it down.

00:00:56.802 --> 00:00:59.111
I got to my core list of books

00:00:59.111 --> 00:01:01.262
that I read and I reread

00:01:01.262 --> 00:01:03.967
and have given me so much value.

00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.821
And today, I wanted to
share them with you,

00:01:05.821 --> 00:01:08.540
and hopefully it transforms
the way you think

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:11.623
and transforms your business as well.

00:01:14.662 --> 00:01:16.483
Okay, well, that was awkward.

00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:18.779
(clears throat) Test, one, two, one, two.

00:01:18.779 --> 00:01:22.166
At number seven is The Fred
Factor by Mark Sanborne,

00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:25.330
and this is a book about
delighting your customers.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:27.390
It tells the story about
a postman named Fred,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.033
who goes over and above to
always delight his customers,

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:32.265
so the people on his route,

00:01:32.265 --> 00:01:33.723
and you think about being a postman,

00:01:33.723 --> 00:01:34.923
it could be a boring job.

00:01:34.923 --> 00:01:36.423
You're doing the same thing over and over

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:38.252
and over and over again, every single day,

00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:41.985
but Fred finds a way to
get to know his customers,

00:01:41.985 --> 00:01:44.921
to watch over their houses
when he knows they're not home

00:01:44.921 --> 00:01:45.754
or on vacation,

00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:48.448
to always look for ways to
delight and surprise them.

00:01:48.448 --> 00:01:52.023
And so, if you have a business
where you personally are

00:01:52.023 --> 00:01:53.420
involved in dealing with customers,

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.900
which will be most people,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.290
or if you have people on your team

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:59.304
who are responsible for
dealing with customers,

00:01:59.304 --> 00:02:00.482
give them this book.

00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:01.361
It's a short read.

00:02:01.361 --> 00:02:02.387
Look at that.

00:02:02.387 --> 00:02:03.718
Look how thin that is.

00:02:03.718 --> 00:02:06.255
It's like not even 100 pages.

00:02:06.255 --> 00:02:07.088
How many pages?

00:02:07.088 --> 00:02:07.921
100 pages.

00:02:07.921 --> 00:02:09.249
Just over 100 pages.

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:10.513
Super fast read.

00:02:10.513 --> 00:02:12.576
It'll change your mindset on
how to work with customers.

00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:13.493
Pick it up.

00:02:15.857 --> 00:02:19.274
At number six is The Go-Giver by Bob Burg

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.688
and John David Mann.

00:02:21.688 --> 00:02:24.217
This is an awesome book,
another quick read.

00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:26.134
It is, what, 125 pages.

00:02:27.535 --> 00:02:29.221
Pretty easy to sift through.

00:02:29.221 --> 00:02:31.240
You could probably get through
in one sitting as well,

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.869
and this book is all about giving

00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:37.009
and helps change your
mindset from being a taker

00:02:37.009 --> 00:02:37.995
and saying here are my goals

00:02:37.995 --> 00:02:39.886
and I got to go out and take what I can

00:02:39.886 --> 00:02:42.115
to realizing that to
accomplish your goals,

00:02:42.115 --> 00:02:44.080
you have to give to other people,

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.207
help others do what they're trying to do,

00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:47.706
help others accomplish their goals.

00:02:47.706 --> 00:02:50.192
And in turn, they're going
to come back and help you,

00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:52.877
and often the path to reaching your goal

00:02:52.877 --> 00:02:54.575
is totally unexpected.

00:02:54.575 --> 00:02:57.204
And it's going to come as a
result of helping other people.

00:02:57.204 --> 00:02:59.687
So, it totally changed my mindset

00:02:59.687 --> 00:03:02.027
of what I needed to do in business

00:03:02.027 --> 00:03:03.969
and not just go and try to reach

00:03:03.969 --> 00:03:05.600
and take my goals,

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.151
but to help others along the path.

00:03:08.151 --> 00:03:09.550
It's an inspiring story.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.560
You can't help but feel
great after reading it.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.742
You can't help but feel
changed after reading it.

00:03:13.742 --> 00:03:15.674
You want to go out and make
the world a better place.

00:03:15.674 --> 00:03:18.626
It's an uplifting,
positive, awesome story.

00:03:18.626 --> 00:03:23.163
Coming in at number six, go
check it out, The Go-Giver.

00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:25.705
Coming in at number five is Donald Trump,

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.047
The Art of the Deal.

00:03:27.047 --> 00:03:28.587
This is one of my favorite books

00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:31.226
