00:10:12.239 --> 00:10:16.823
And at the core, this book
is a productivity book.

00:10:16.823 --> 00:10:19.131
It'll teach you how to
automate, how to delegate,

00:10:19.131 --> 00:10:21.515
how to eliminate, how to outsource,

00:10:21.515 --> 00:10:23.951
how to apply the 80-20
rule to your business,

00:10:23.951 --> 00:10:27.374
how to be more efficient,
get more stuff done

00:10:27.374 --> 00:10:29.986
so that then you can go live
the life of your dreams.

00:10:29.986 --> 00:10:32.118
It teaches you a lot about productivity,

00:10:32.118 --> 00:10:33.515
and since reading this book,

00:10:33.515 --> 00:10:35.596
I've become a productivity nut

00:10:35.596 --> 00:10:38.217
and have applied a lot of the strategies

00:10:38.217 --> 00:10:40.211
that Tim suggests in this book

00:10:40.211 --> 00:10:41.494
to my life, to my business.

00:10:41.494 --> 00:10:43.756
And it's had dramatic impact.

00:10:43.756 --> 00:10:46.609
The other thing though
that you learn from it is

00:10:46.609 --> 00:10:49.192
Tim thinks way outside the box,

00:10:50.304 --> 00:10:52.924
and even now, a lot of the strategies here

00:10:52.924 --> 00:10:55.882
are still way, way, way,
way outside the box.

00:10:55.882 --> 00:10:58.398
And you don't even realize

00:10:58.398 --> 00:11:00.532
that some of these things are possible.

00:11:00.532 --> 00:11:02.266
That was what I was so
excited and interested

00:11:02.266 --> 00:11:03.694
in reading from him,

00:11:03.694 --> 00:11:06.711
and this is the extended
and updated version.

00:11:06.711 --> 00:11:07.619
So, I got the original,

00:11:07.619 --> 00:11:09.284
and then, I bought the updated version.

00:11:09.284 --> 00:11:10.616
And if he puts another one out,

00:11:10.616 --> 00:11:12.867
I'm going to buy that one
too 'cause it's awesome.

00:11:12.867 --> 00:11:16.763
But it challenges you
to think differently.

00:11:16.763 --> 00:11:19.705
It challenges you to step
outside your comfort zone.

00:11:19.705 --> 00:11:21.646
It challenges you to look for other ways

00:11:21.646 --> 00:11:22.742
to accomplish a goal

00:11:22.742 --> 00:11:24.487
that you may not have
ever thought possible.

00:11:24.487 --> 00:11:26.593
So, on top of all the
great productivity advice

00:11:26.593 --> 00:11:28.405
that you get, that I get from it

00:11:28.405 --> 00:11:30.312
and taken notes and read through it,

00:11:30.312 --> 00:11:34.308
it also makes you think more creatively,

00:11:34.308 --> 00:11:35.856
makes you look for other options.

00:11:35.856 --> 00:11:36.878
And as an entrepreneur,

00:11:36.878 --> 00:11:39.760
that's what you're going to
have to do to be successful

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.893
because chances are it's
not just going to be

00:11:41.893 --> 00:11:43.388
this straight path to success.

00:11:43.388 --> 00:11:45.749
It's going to be a
crazy, wild, bumpy ride,

00:11:45.749 --> 00:11:47.066
and you can't just do the things

00:11:47.066 --> 00:11:48.423
that everybody else does.

00:11:48.423 --> 00:11:49.483
You got to be creative.

00:11:49.483 --> 00:11:50.705
You got to step outside the box.

00:11:50.705 --> 00:11:53.168
That's what this book helps you do.

00:11:53.168 --> 00:11:54.599
Tim Ferriss, The 4-Hour Workweek,

00:11:54.599 --> 00:11:56.809
the number one book for all entrepreneurs.

00:11:56.809 --> 00:11:58.226
You must read it.

00:11:59.302 --> 00:12:00.683
